                <pb facs="0105" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v23/pg72"/>

                <head>54. Telegram From the Station in the Congo to the Central Intelligence
                        Agency<anchor n="1" xml:id="d54-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Leopoldville</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1961-01-12">January 12,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>0625 (In 30010).</p>
                <p>1. [<hi rendition="#italic">cryptonym not declassified</hi>]<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d54-f2"/> situation deteriorating rapidly. Troops and police most
                    resentful because pay low as compared officers and govt leaders. Per [Embassy]
                    cables, police were on verge mutiny 10 Jan. Many local sources say discontent
                    continuing mount but station not able substantiate at present.</p>
                <p>2. [COS] returned Leop morning 12 Jan on same
                    plane [Identity 1]. Latter talked with
                        [Mobutu] by phone 11 Jan. Said it
                    his opinion Leop garrison will mutiny within two or three days unless drastic
                    action <pb facs="0106" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/> taken satisfy complaints.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d54-f3"/> In reply question said only suggestion at present is
                    offer troops special combat bonus to put down Gizenga “rebellion.” However said
                    no GOC funds available this purpose. Literally
                    begged [COS] obtain ODYOKE funds meet this need, pointing out troop mutiny almost
                    certainly would end [Mobutu] control
                        CNA and bring about [Lumumba] return power. [Identity 1] estimates would take about one
                    million dollars per month for several months to achieve objective. He recognizes
                    this not good solution for in way this is accepting CNA blackmail. But believes it better than letting matters drift
                    and facing certain failure [<hi rendition="#italic">cryptonym not
                        declassified</hi>]<anchor n="4" xml:id="d54-f4"/> objectives. Station
                    concurs.</p>
                <p>3. COS and Ambassador seeing [Identity 1] 1500Z, 12 Jan. [COS] also trying contact [Mobutu] and other [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >cryptonym not declassified</hi>] leaders to get reading. This message sent
                    warn HQS serious problem exists and to urge
                    immediate KUBARK liaison and discussion this
                    problem. Believe could insert funds clandestinely via [Mobutu], [Identity 1] if necessary.</p>
                <p>4. Will cable Station and [Embassy] views on request soonest.</p>
                <p>End of message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d54-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d54-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency Files, Job 78–00435R, DDO/ISS Files, Box 1,
                    Folder 6, [<hi rendition="#italic">cryptonym not declassified</hi>] Ops. Secret; Rybat; [<hi rendition="#italic">cryptonym not declassified</hi>];
                    Operational Immediate. Received at 1741Z.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d54-f2" n="2" xml:id="d54-f2-content">
                <p>CIA political action program in support of
                    moderate, anti-Lumumba leaders in the
                    Congo [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>].</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d54-f3" n="3" xml:id="d54-f3-content">
                <p>Part of this sentence is quoted in <hi rendition="#italic">Interim Report</hi> p.
                    49.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d54-f4" n="4" xml:id="d54-f4-content">
                <p>See footnote 2.</p>
            </note>
